/target/
/.idea/
/.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.tmp
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Runtime log of the five-minute disk guardian (scripts/disk-guardian.sh)
.disk-guardian.log
# Local reference corpus is never source input and must never be committed.
refference/
# Built macOS client bundle (regenerate: packaging/macos/build-deck-app.sh)
Arcen Deck.app/
.gstack/
# Local key material. Never commit.
/keys/
# Provisioning profiles contain sensitive team credentials — store outside git or in AppleCerts/
clients/macos/*.provisionprofile

# Release artefacts assembled by hand; binaries are never committed.
dist/*
!dist/README.md

# Lab installer output (built binaries, never committed)
/dist-installers/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private, never-published working material.
#
# This repository is public. Anything that names real infrastructure, accounts
# or credentials belongs in one of the paths below, NOT in tracked files:
#   - test-host inventories and lab addresses
#   - notary profile names, certificate common names, signing private keys
#   - deployment runbooks against real machines
#
# The signing/notarisation PROCEDURE is documented and tracked in
# docs/operations/macos-signing.md; only the VALUES live here.
#
# Note: these paths are not backed up by git. Keep a second copy of anything
# you cannot regenerate (certificates and private keys especially).
#
# .github/ is deliberately NOT ignored: CODEOWNERS, FUNDING.yml, release.yml and
# workflows/ are functional configuration that GitHub reads from the repository,
# so ignoring it would silently disable CI, review routing and the funding link.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.local/
*.private.md
